              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Good options. Useful often."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Blue"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Fantastic options, often essential\n\t\tto the function of your character. Useful very frequently."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "depths": [
            0,
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "itemKinds": [
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered"
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The advice offered below is based on the current "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "State of the 2014 DnD 5e Character Optimization Meta",
              "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/characters/state-of-the-meta/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " as of when the article was last updated. Keep in mind that the state of the meta periodically changes as new source materials are released, and the article will be updated accordingly as time allows."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-disclaimer-4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "We will not include 3rd-party content, Unearthed Arcnaa content, or homebrew in guides for official content because we can’t assume that your game will allow them."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Locathah Classes (Customizable Origins)",
      "sourceAnchor": "classes-custom-origin",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-classes-custom-origin-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "This section assumes that you’re using the option “"
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Customizing Your Origin",
              "href": "https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/tcoe/character-options#CustomizingYourOrigin"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "” rules presented in Tasha’s Cauldron of Everything. If you’re not using those rules, scroll down to the next section."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-artificer",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Artificer",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-artificer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-artificer-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Despite their exceptional durability, the Artificer doesn’t get protection\n\tfrom the conditions handled by Leviathan Will until you get Stroke of Genius\n\tat high levels. Artificers also seem uniquely well-suited to produce a\n\tsolution to the Locathah’s Limited Amphibiousness, though it doesn’t exactly\n\ttake a genius to arrive at a bath tub as a solution."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-barbarian",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Barbarian",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-barbarian",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-barbarian-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Barbarians have poor Will saves, making charm, fear, and sleep effects\n\textremely dangerous for them. Leviathan Will provides some much-needed\n\tprotection. Two skills also help to make the Barbarian useful outside of\n\tcombat, which is a much-needed improvement."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-bard",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Bard",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-bard",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-bard-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Two additional skills are great on a class that’s so well-suited to using\n\tskills, and Leviathan Will provides some helpful protections for a class\n\tthat’s generally frail."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-cleric",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Cleric",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-cleric",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-cleric-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Leviathan Will is a great way to keep your party’s primary healer from being\n\ttaken out of a fight by one spell or special ability."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-druid",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Druid",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-druid",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-druid-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Leviathan Will is a great way to keep your party’s primary healer from being\n\ttaken out of a fight by one spell or special ability. It also appears to work\n\twhile using Wild Shape, but I’m not totally certain."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-fighter",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Fighter",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-fighter",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-fighter-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Fighters have poor Will saves, making charm, fear, and sleep effects\n\textremely dangerous for them. Leviathan Will provides some much-needed\n\tprotection. Two skills also help to make the Fighter useful outside of combat,\n\twhich is a much-needed improvement."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-monk",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Monk",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-monk",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-monk-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Two skills helps close the skill gap between the Monk and the Rogue, making\n\tit easier to serve as your party’s Scout. Leviathan Will coupled with the\n\tMonk’s saving throws will make you extremely resiliant, especially at high\n\tlevels once you have proficiency in all saving throws."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-paladin",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Paladin",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-paladin",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-paladin-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Paladins are already extremely resilient, so you’ll be basically untouchable\n\tonce you get Aura of Protection. Two skills help to expand beyond Face skills,\n\tallowing you explore other options."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-ranger",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Ranger",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-ranger",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-ranger-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Two skills helps close the skill gap between the Ranger and the Rogue, making\n\tit easier to serve as your party’s Scout."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-rogue",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Rogue",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-rogue",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-rogue-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Two extra skills allow you to cover a broad range of skill-based roles, and\n\tLeviathan Will protects from you from things that don’t touch your already\n\texcellent Dexterity saves."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-sorcerer",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Sorcerer",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-sorcerer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-sorcerer-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Two extra skills help to expand beyond Face skills, and Leviathan Will\n\tprovides some durability which is difficult to replace with spells."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-warlock",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Warlock",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-warlock",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-warlock-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Two extra skills help to expand beyond Face skills, and Leviathan Will\n\tprovides some durability which is difficult to replace with spells."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-custom-origin-wizard",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-custom-origin",
      "heading": "Wizard",
      "sourceAnchor": "custom-origin-wizard",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-custom-origin-wizard-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Leviathan Will provides some durability which is difficult to replace with\n\tspells. There aren’t many Intelligence-based skills, so the Wizard’s skill\n\toptions are generally limited."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Locathah Classes (Default Rules)",
      "sourceAnchor": "classes-default",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-classes-default-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "This section assumes that you’re "
            },
            {
              "type": "emphasis",
              "text": "not"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " using the option “Customizing Your Origin” rules presented in Tasha’s Cauldron of Everything or the updated version of the race published in Mordenkainen’s Monsters of the Multiverse. If you are using those rules, scroll up to the previous section."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-default-artificer",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Artificer",
      "sourceAnchor": "default-artificer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-default-artificer-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "No Intelligence increase."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-default-barbarian",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Barbarian",
      "sourceAnchor": "default-barbarian",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-default-barbarian-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Increase to both Strength and Dexterity are a great start for the Barbarian,\n\tand the Locathah’s additional skills help to broaden your capabilities beyond\n\thitting stuff. Natural Armor will be redundant with Unarmored Defense, but\n\tthat’s perfectly fine. Leviathan Will will also help protect from a lot of\n\tnon-damage problems which could take you out of a fight."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-default-bard",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Bard",
      "sourceAnchor": "default-bard",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-default-bard-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Lacking a Charisma increase is hard, but if you don’t use your spellcasting\n\toffensively you can do reasonably well. Martial subclasses like College of\n\tValor and College of Swords are your best bet."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-default-cleric",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Cleric",
      "sourceAnchor": "default-cleric",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-default-cleric-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Without a Wisdom increase, the Cleric is a hard choice. You could try for a\n\tmartial build like War Domain or something, but you’ll still lag considerably\n\tcompared to other clerics."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-default-druid",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Druid",
      "sourceAnchor": "default-druid",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-default-druid-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Without a Wisdom increase, the Druid is a hard choice but maybe not as hard\n\tas the Cleric. Leviathan Will looks like it would work while using Wild Shape,\n\twhich is an interesting defensive option, and the two free skills are always\n\tgreat. You’ll lag behind other druids in terms of spellcasting, but Circle of\n\tthe Moon could still work well if you avoid offensive spells."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-default-fighter",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Fighter",
      "sourceAnchor": "default-fighter",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-default-fighter-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Increases to both Strength and Dexterity mean that you’ve got flexibility in\n\tyour weapon choices, but Strength is likely still the better choice. Between a\n\tStrength increase and proficiency in Athletics, not focusing on Strength seems\n\tlike a lost opportunity."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-default-monk",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Monk",
      "sourceAnchor": "default-monk",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-default-monk-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Dexterity increase and the additional skills works great for the Monk,\n\tand Leviathan Will offers some helpful defenses. Strength and Natural Armor\n\twill go unused, but that’s fine. I think the Monk isn’t quite as appealing to\n\tthe Locathah because it doesn’t capitalize on the Locathah’s traits as well as\n\tthe Fighter or similar classes, but it’s still a good option."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-default-paladin",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Paladin",
      "sourceAnchor": "default-paladin",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-default-paladin-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Dexterity is much less useful for the Paladin than for the Barbarian and the\n\tFighter, but otherwise the Locathah makes a fine paladin. Leviathan Will\n\tcovers several conditions not already handled by paladin class features, which\n\tmakes you very hard to incapacitate."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-default-ranger",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Ranger",
      "sourceAnchor": "default-ranger",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-default-ranger-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Increases to both Strength and Dexterity make it easier to build a\n\tStrength-based build because you can manage decent scores in both at 1st\n\tlevel. Two additional skills help close the skill gap with Rogue, too. Given\n\tthe choice between the Ranger and the Rogue for a stealty Locathah, I would go\n\tfor the the Ranger."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-default-rogue",
      "parentSectionId": "section-classes-default",
      "heading": "Rogue",
      "sourceAnchor": "default-rogue",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-default-rogue-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Dexterity increase is all that you really need, but not needing armor is\n\tnice and the additional skills are always welcome on a high-skilled class like\n\tthe Rogue."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
